  "title": "Flux through a surface.",
  "body": " Flux through a surface   Consider the velocity field . Let be the flat rectangular surface lying in the plane , with and , oriented with outward unit normal . Calculate the flux of through .    On the surface we have , so   The flux is therefore   Notice that only the -component of contributes, since points purely in the -direction; the flux measures how much fluid crosses per unit time in that direction.   "
