  "body": " Uniqueness of solutions  You may be wondering whether a potential found by the method of images, with its 'fictitious' image points, is the only solution. It is unique (up to a constant) once we prescribe the singularities in the flow region (sources and vortices, with their strengths), the no-flux condition on the walls, and the behaviour at infinity, e.g. . This follows from the uniqueness of solutions to Laplace's equation with this type of boundary condition (a Neumann problem).  The condition at infinity matters. In the examples above, adding a uniform flow parallel to the wall, (for which is constant on ), still satisfies the no-flux condition, but changes the flow far from the source or vortex.  "
